        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7781f4f7-698d-570b-9c87-4afcf235b40a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Loretta Young, Henry Wilcoxon, Cecil B. DeMille\n- Films: The Crusades, The Farmer's Daughter, Come to the Stable\n- Companies: Paramount Pictures\n- Roles: Berengaria of Navarre, Richard I of England\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Actress, Oscar nomination\n\nFacts:\n- Loretta Young was born on January 6, 1913, and died on August 12, 2000.\n- The Crusades is a 1935 American historical adventure film produced and directed by Cecil B. DeMille and originally released by Paramount Pictures.\n- In The Crusades, Loretta Young played Berengaria of Navarre and Henry Wilcoxon played Richard I of England.\n- Loretta Young was an American actress and singer.\n- Loretta Young won the 1948 Academy Award for Best Actress for her role in the 1947 film The Farmer's Daughter.\n- Loretta Young received an Oscar nomination in 1949 for her role in Come to the Stable.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
